# This approach is already correct, according to the MAGeCK Flute paper, the p-value and FDR determines whether the beta score is different from 0 (Wang et al, 2019)
# Similarly, the ‘wald-p-value’ and ‘wald-fdr’ are the P value and FDR, respectively, calculated by the Wald test to determine whether the corresponding ‘beta score’ differs substantially from zero in the MAGeCK MLE model
# hence if we dont filter the data based on pvalue and FDR, that is totally fine, the actual thing that we should look at is the beta score as the effect size
# it is totally different for MAGeCK RRA, where the pvalue and FDR corresponds to the scores for each genes, as stated in MAGeCKflute paper, the MAGeCK RRA also outputs a P value or false-discovery rate (FDR) for the scores of each gene. Hence filtering would be required if we use MAGeCK RRA
# For original Cellecta 150K library use this
# M1_gdata <- function_import_flute_mle('../Chapter-1-data/02_MAGeCK_MLE_Analysis/MAGeCKFlute_M1_53K_Flute_MLE/QC/M1_53K_Flute_MLE_processed_data.txt',
#                                       '../Chapter-1-data/02_MAGeCK_MLE_Analysis/Module_1_Cellecta_150K_norm_mageck_complete_analysis/Module_1_Cellecta_150K_norm_mageck_mle/M1_Cellecta_150K_norm.gene_summary.txt')
#
